{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Thread the probe allowlist into project-criterion routing\n\n## Problem (verified at origin/main cc69cc1179)\n\n`ProductionBatchRunner.run` fans activated `project.<name>` criteria into the Pass-1 set via\n`_project_criteria(ctx, exclude)` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py:112`,\ndefined at `:257`). That helper calls `orchestrator.route_criteria(ctx)`, which has NO probe\nnotion.\n\nUnder PROBE MODE (the drift-refresh tripwire), the built-in set is forced to the tiny\nallowlist `E4`+`G1G2` — `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py:254-263` does\n`included = {cid for cid in effective if cid in probe}`. But built-ins reach the runner through\n`req.criteria` while project criteria are re-routed independently, so an activated project\ncriterion is ALSO evaluated during a probe: extra billable LLM calls on what is meant to be the\ncheap probe. Harmless to the verdict today (the drift comparison keys off E4/G1G2 only), and the\nexisting caveat at `production_batch_runner.py:265-269` names this ticket as the follow-up.\n\n## Approach\n\nThe probe allowlist already reaches the workflow as gate input `probe_criteria`\n(`gates/plan-review.yaml:24`, threaded to the `assemble` step at `:54`). Deliver it to the batch\nstep through the EXISTING generic seam — a batch step's `with:` is resolved once by the\ninterpreter (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/interpreter.py:376-396`) into\n`BatchRunRequest.with_inputs`, which this runner already reads three keys from (`:155`, `:166`,\n`:173`). So NO change to the generic `BatchRunRequest` dataclass, and no plan-review concept\nleaks into the seam: a runner that ignores the key (e.g. `DefaultBatchRunner`) is unaffected.\n\nSuppression semantics MIRROR `workflow_ops`: keep only ids present in the allowlist. Since a\n`project.` id is never in the E4/G1G2 probe set, that is suppression in practice, but the\nfilter — rather than a blanket \"return nothing when probing\" — stays correct if the allowlist\never grows.\n\n## Changes\n\n1. `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml:60-62` — add\n   `probe_criteria: ${{ inputs.probe_criteria }}` to the `finders` batch `with:`.\n2. `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py:257` — `_project_criteria` grows a\n   third parameter `probe` (an id collection, default empty). When non-empty, the returned\n   project criteria are filtered to ids in `probe`.\n3. `production_batch_runner.py:112` — pass `req.with_inputs.get(\"probe_criteria\")`.\n4. `production_batch_runner.py:265-269` — replace the caveat paragraph with a description of\n   the implemented behaviour (the ticket reference goes away with the caveat).\n\n## Tests\n\n- `tests/unit/test_criteria_overlay.py:234-238` (existing project fan-in test) — extend: with a\n  probe allowlist of `E4`/`G1G2`, `_project_criteria` returns `([], [])` for the same activated\n  `project.no-print` overlay that fans in when NOT probing. Same-fixture pair, so it fails\n  before the change and passes after. Its two existing calls pass `exclude=` by KEYWORD, so a\n  defaulted new parameter leaves them working.\n- **Monkeypatch stub population.** `_project_criteria` is stubbed in tests via\n  `monkeypatch.setattr`, which Serena cannot see; grepping the symbol as a STRING\n  (`grep -rn '_project_criteria' tests/`) enumerates the WHOLE population — exactly TWO\n  2-positional-arg stubs, both `lambda ctx, seen: ([], [])`:\n  `tests/unit/test_pass1_finder_model.py:103` AND `tests/unit/test_model_class_ladder.py:143`.\n  Once the call site at `production_batch_runner.py:112` passes a third argument, EITHER\n  un-updated stub raises `TypeError`. Both are updated to accept it. (The remaining `tests/`\n  hits are unrelated: docstring mentions in `test_bug_blast_radius_escalation_ad0d.py:16,174`\n  and code-review's separate `_validated_project_criteria`.)\n- A YAML-level assertion that the `finders` batch `with:` carries `probe_criteria`, so the\n  wiring cannot regress silently while the unit test still passes.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] With a non-empty `probe_criteria`, `_project_criteria` returns no activated project\n      criterion whose id is outside the allowlist. Worked example: the\n      `project.no-print` overlay fixture + allowlist `[\"E4\",\"G1G2\"]` yields `([], [])`.\n- [ ] With an empty/absent `probe_criteria`, the fan-in is byte-identical to today: the same\n      fixture yields `project.no-print` in the single-turn set (normal full review unchanged).\n- [ ] `gates/plan-review.yaml`'s `finders` batch `with:` passes `inputs.probe_criteria`.\n- [ ] `BatchRunRequest` (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/runners.py:61`) is UNCHANGED — no\n      plan-review-specific field on the generic seam.\n- [ ] The `production_batch_runner.py` caveat naming this ticket is gone, replaced by a\n      description of the implemented behaviour.\n- [ ] NO 2-positional-arg `_project_criteria` stub remains: `grep -rn '_project_criteria' tests/`\n      shows both `test_pass1_finder_model.py` and `test_model_class_ladder.py` stubs accepting\n      the third argument. This fails while ANY instance remains un-updated.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` passes.\n- [ ] The touched unit tests pass: `pytest tests/unit/test_criteria_overlay.py\n      tests/unit/test_pass1_finder_model.py tests/unit/test_model_class_ladder.py`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786558465606331001,"uuid":"1cf43c1c-9d2f-47fe-986d-7c713e2c8f1d"}